{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545738-artefacts","id":1545738,"title":"Artefacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-12T04:24:30-08:00","id":1545738,"title":"Artefacts","content":"Based mostly on forged by dragon fire.<br /> Is there a difference in cost of a artefact that changes the target human to chicken to an artefact that changes the target to anything the user desire?<br /> The main advantage of artefacts is they require just 1 success to work. But should it be possible to create artefacts with so broad powers without extra cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T12:41:49-08:00","id":1546147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545738-artefacts#post1545738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a difference in cost of a artefact that changes the target human to chicken to an artefact that changes the target to anything the user desire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, AFAIK.<br /> <br /> The only limit it's that Wonders can be imbued with Rotes, not with Spheres. But that's not as real a limit as it seems: while Rotes are defined as concrete and repeatable Effects, in truth there's no rule limiting how concrete or open-ended these have to be. And in the books you have named examples of Rotes that are VERY open ended, to the point you could cast them tens of times w/o ever repeating the result<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main advantage of artefacts is they require just 1 success to work. But should it be possible to create artefacts with so broad powers without extra cost? </div> </div> </div>I don't think that was intended. Looking at the artifact examples, you don't have &quot;blasters of all types of energy&quot;. You have flame-breathing candy, plasma cannons. I've seen Wonders that allow you to change into one animal, but none to transform into anything.<br /> <br /> It seems like an unwritten rule (perhaps more of an unwritten advice) that Wonders should have very defined effects, rather than undefined <br /> <br /> This is part of a family of things that have irked me a lot for the longest time. I think my first post about Mage on Internet ever was me being aghast at this on FbDF: The limits of artifacts in terms of Sphere requisites are cristal clear (well, as cristal as something can be in Mage), but their limit in &quot;potency&quot; (something usually detailed by the Arete roll) it's less than vague - it's <b>undefined.</b><br /> <br /> The simplest truth it's that Mage wants you to go trough this as a very intuition-based, <i>wibbily-wobbily</i>, Paradigm thing. Let the player define what they want to do in the terms of the Paradigm, then let them do it. While all of Mage it's like this to some extent, Wonders it's like this squared - sometimes I <b>wonder </b><i>why there's even rules</i>. <br /> <br /> So, really there's no limit to how powerful, broad or vast a basic Wonder can get. Other than what you yourself think Wonders should look like. Do as thou wilt shall be the whole of the law.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T22:23:28-08:00","id":1546180,"title":"","content":"So i guess i have to cook my own solution here. Thank you for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T08:23:42-08:00","id":1547545,"title":"","content":"By raw, there is no extra cost. There is no differemce in cost from am artifact and a (considerably more powerful) talisman, at char creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T17:21:12-08:00","id":1547707,"title":"","content":"If they're forged by dragon-fire, then that should give it a some tass. (That may be a book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}